From 61a3c156d2ebb8267e21acff091cac363c608471 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:38:29 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Let a layout file drop duplicate recommendation rows, hide
 rows and order them

The Discover page shows every source's rows interleaved, one per source per pass,
and there is no say over which rows exist or which come first. With a Subsonic
server and the library plugin both enabled the same row appears twice ("New
Albums" next to "Recently Added Albums": both carry the translation key
recently_added_albums), and the Last.fm and trending rows crowd out the
library's own.

recommendations_layout.json in the data directory takes that over, read on every
request so an edit applies without a restart:

  dedupe  keep one row per translation key, the library's own by preference
          (on unless switched off, since a row twice is never wanted)
  hide    patterns for rows not to offer at all
  order   patterns for rows to put first, in that order; the rest keep their
          interleaved order after them

A pattern is a case-insensitive fnmatch against provider:item_id, item_id,
translation_key and name:<row name>. A missing or malformed file changes nothing
but the dedupe. The helper has no imports from the server, so its test loads it
by path and runs without the server's dependencies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
